{#
    A present value's saved form (SCE Accepted Subset §2.15, docs/adr/0045), as a Swift machine
    reads it back (`SavedValues` of the runtime). One text for a machine's `readSavedVariables`
    (`swift/saved_state.swift.jinja2`) and for a test component's read of its module parameters
    (`swift/state_machine.swift.jinja2`, docs/SCE_TEST_PROFILE.md §11.5), which reads a value as a
    restored variable of its type is read. The Swift twin of `_macros/c_saved_value.jinja2`.
#}

{#- A present value read as its type says: an enum by its own type, a record by its own `fromSaved`, a byte
   string and a text held to the bound the machine keeps them to, anything else by the function its
   `sce:type` names. `shape` is `enum`, `record`, `union` or `scalar`; a union reads itself as a record does
   (docs/adr/0092, section 6.1 item 7). #}
{%- macro saved_present(type, shape, value, what, bound) -%}
{%- if shape == 'enum' -%}
try SavedValues.enumeration({{ value }}, {{ what }}, as: {{ type }}.self)
{%- elif shape == 'record' or shape == 'union' -%}
try {{ type }}.fromSaved({{ value }}, {{ what }})
{%- elif type == 'bytes' -%}
try SavedValues.bytes({{ value }}, {{ what }}{% if bound is not none %}, capacity: {{ bound }}{% endif %})
{%- elif type == 'string' -%}
try SavedValues.string({{ value }}, {{ what }}{% if bound is not none %}, capacity: {{ bound }}{% endif %})
{%- else -%}
try SavedValues.{{ type }}({{ value }}, {{ what }})
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
